ClipCut third-party notices

Upstream project

ClipCut is a rebrand of ClearCut (https://github.com/SysAdminDoc/ClearCut), an open-source
Android video editor released under the MIT licence. Copyright (c) 2026 SysAdminDoc. The
editing engine, AI pipelines, exporters and asset formats in this repository originate
there; ClipCut's own changes are the product name, application id, iconography, theme
naming and documentation.

FFmpegKitNext / FFmpeg

ClipCut bundles a source-pinned LGPL-3.0-or-later build of FFmpegKitNext 8.1.0 with FFmpeg 8.1.2, OpenH264, libass, and the supporting libraries recorded in third_party/ffmpeg-kit-next/native-lock.json. The exact upstream commit is 3e223118e6e8fb6208693ecf3952e77cd096f587 and the reproducible build command is ./nix-android.sh -p android-r27d --enable-libass --enable-libjxl --enable-android-media-codec --enable-android-zlib --enable-openh264 --jobs=8. The ClipCut security patch disables the VobSub, TDSC, MACE6, ADX/AAX, PNG/APNG, RASC, IAMF, and LCL/ZLIB components named in the lockfile's required advisory inventory.

The Android package includes the upstream license resources under res/raw/license*.txt and res/raw/source.txt, plus ClipCut's exact source recipe under res/raw/ffmpeg_kit_next_source_offer.txt. Keep those resources and the corresponding-source access available with redistributed builds.

DeepFilterNet

ClipCut may bundle io.github.kaleyravideo:android-deepfilternet:0.0.8 for on-device audio noise reduction. The Kaleyra Android AAR is licensed under Apache License 2.0 and is built on the upstream DeepFilterNet project, whose code and model weights are available under MIT or Apache License 2.0 at the user's option. Keep the relevant Apache/MIT notices with redistributed builds that include the DeepFilterNet native library and bundled model.

gl-transitions

ClipCut bundles transition shaders derived from gl-transitions
(https://github.com/gl-transitions/gl-transitions), licensed under the MIT licence,
Copyright (c) 2017-present gl-transitions contributors. There are 212 of them, and each
shader remains under the licence of the individual author named in its upstream header
(overwhelmingly MIT, a few CC-BY-3.0); the per-transition author and licence strings are
preserved verbatim in app/src/main/assets/gltransitions/catalog.json, which ships with the
APK. The shaders were mechanically converted from GLSL ES 1.00 to GLSL ES 3.00 by
tools/gen_gltransitions.py and are rendered by
app/src/main/java/com/clipcut/editor/engine/gltransition/GlTransitionEffect.kt. Two
upstream transitions (DisplacementMap, LumaWipe) are not bundled because they require an
extra user-supplied texture.

